  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Primary Health Care provision for vulnerable populations affected by food insecurity and malnutrition in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The overall objective (Impact) of the Action is to contribute to improve the health conditions of vulnerable populations affected by extreme poverty, food insecurity and malnutrition in Sudan including IDPs, refugees and Host Communities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The specific objective (Outcome) of the Action is to increase sustainable access to and demand for quality Primary Health Care (PHC), Nutrition, Psycho-Social Support (PSS) and Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services in targeted States, including for host communities, Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) and refugees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 1.1: Primary Health Care (PHC), Nutrition and Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services at Primary Health Care (PHC) centres and community levels are improved, including for IDPs, refugees and host communities, with focus on women, girls, and persons living with disability (PLwD).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Output 1.2: Management capacity and accountability of local health systems are strengthened.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Output 1.3: Socio-cultural behavioural and gender barriers to health and nutrition are reduced.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
